    mir_enum_payload_inline_none_lowered_as_nil_2026-11-10, P1, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "stage2 native: inline None payload arg reaches MIR as NilLit, rejected as nil outside unsafe", src/compiler/60.mir_opt/mir_opt/string_builder_opt.spl, 197, test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/enum_payload_inline_none_imported_optional_struct_spec.spl, 2026-11-10, 2026-11-10, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    mir_enum_payload_inline_none_lowered_as_nil_2026-11-10, 0, "2026-11-10: NOT reproduced. Interpreter MIR spec (direct, struct-field, if-val arm in while, match arm) all admit None; stage2_new4.exe native-build of 1- and 2-module repros of the exact string_builder_opt shape links and runs. Source review: no frontend/HIR/codec path rewrites None to NilLit (HIR emits NamedVar; codec round-trips NamedVar). Entry-closure stage2 build of string_builder_opt crashed in MIR shard (invalid array handle) before reaching it. Next: capture the stage3 HIR shard for compiler.mir_opt.string_builder_opt and decode the arg node. Call-site workaround lane is separate."
    mir_enum_payload_inline_none_lowered_as_nil_2026-11-10, 1, "2026-11-10 (lane p2-inline-none): root-cause narrowing. Every failing site (Call(None,..), HirTypeKind.Array(elem, None), HirExprKind.IntLit(v, None)) is a 2+-arg payload and so routes through box_tuple_payload (switch_operators_calls.spl), the ONE constructor path that re-read values[vi] four times AFTER lower_declared_enum_payload_expression had allocated (compat check, trace, message, span); the 1-arg path binds `val value = payload_values[i]` once and never failed. In the sharded stage3 build the arg HirExprs are codec-pool values, and re-reading one after allocation is the known native single-read class (expression_core.spl NamedVar arm, cycle-160): the stale re-read decoded as NilLit, so the compat check took the `nil outside unsafe` branch for an inline None. Fix: bind `val value: HirExpr = values[vi]` once per slot and use it for lowering, admission, trace and diagnostic. Interpreter never reproduces (no re-read hazard): new cross-module spec test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/enum_payload_inline_none_imported_optional_struct_spec.spl (facade re-export, class me method, while + if-val + continue, nested call args; inspects MIR: the LocalId? slot word is Const Int(3):i64 and bare nil is still rejected; sibling 2-arg shapes Arr(n, None) and Both(None, None)) 5/5 green before and after; enum_payload_inline_none_contexts_spec.spl 5/5. Native verification pending: rebuild stage2 with this change and drop the two WORKAROUND(stage2-optmerge-void) Bug-A sites in string_builder_opt.spl (kept in place for now)."
